I wrote the plan for 2 tasks. The files are in session_plan/ (task_01.md, task_02.md, issue_responses.md). The commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is gitignored, so git add refused the files. They exist on disk, and the plan command ends in || true, so the harness presumably reads them from there.

Task 1 — Fixes #1145 (product). Setting --temperature, or temperature = in .yoyo.toml, makes every call to the default model (claude-opus-5-5) fail with an HTTP 400. Anthropic dropped temperature for Claude 4.7 and later. Our install docs make it worse, because their example config includes temperature = 0.7.
• A new src/temperature_support.rs module decides which models reject temperature by reading the version number from the model id, not from a hand-kept list. Bedrock ids are mapped first with yoagent's bedrock_anthropic_id.
• agent_builder.rs stops sending temperature to those models and prints a note on stderr once per run.
• The test runs the real config builder: claude-opus-5-5 gets no temperature, and claude-haiku-4-5, which still accepts it, keeps its value.
• Both docs pages get fixed.

Task 2 — Part of #1144 and #1121 (product). yoyo stops offering three dead Claude ids:
• claude-sonnet-4-5: the owner asked for this in #1144 item 3; it retires on 2026-11-30.
• claude-sonnet-4-7: doesn't exist and returns a 404.
• claude-sonnet-4-20250514: retired in June.

They come out of the anthropic and Bedrock known-model lists and the /model completions. A new test checks that none of them appears, and that every listed anthropic id resolves through yoagent's presets with known limits. The task also makes sure the "Available models" list shown after a 404 includes the default model.

Issues filed during planning:
• #1145: the temperature bug. The assessment confirmed it on the built binary; no issue existed yet.
• #1146: an upstream ask for yoagent to know per model whether temperature is accepted, so yoyo's version check can be retired.

